# The image needs the code and the packaging metadata. Everything else is
# either large, secret, or regenerable — and each of those is a reason not to
# ship it.

# The model artifact, above all. It is derived output and is not committed, so
# copying it would mean an image built on a developer's machine bakes whatever
# happened to be in models/ that afternoon, and "which model is serving?" is
# answered with "trust me". The only way a model enters an image is a verified
# fetch from a release tag — docs/design.md §7a, src/inference/fetch.py.
# Locally, mount it instead: docker run -v "$PWD/models:/app/models:ro"
models/

# Data: gigabytes of snapshots and derived frames, none of it needed to serve.
data/
*.db
*.sqlite*

# Experiment tracking: a local cache of runs, rebuildable from the code.
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
mlflow.db

# Host environment: a macOS virtualenv is actively harmful inside a Linux image.
.venv/
venv/
.env

# History and tooling.
.git/
.github/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Tests do not run in the served image; the CI job runs them before it is built.
tests/

# Local working notes, and the planning documents that are not part of the repo.
*.md
!README.md
